# Window rules for KDE Plasma's KWin, placing the lander example's two
# windows side by side when they open: tcs-sim's at the top right, and the
# MOC's at the top left. tcs-sim asks for the top right itself, and says
# how much width that leaves, which the MOC's window fits itself to and
# takes at the top left; but on Wayland a compositor places a window as it
# likes, and KWin's rules are what can place tcs-sim's.
#
# Import it in System Settings, Window Management, Window Rules, Import.
# The positions are in the display's logical pixels -- its pixels divided
# by its scale. tcs-sim's window is about 1188 wide beside the lander, so
# its rule puts it at 519, the right edge of a display 1707 wide, as a
# 3840x2400 display at a scale of 2.25 is: on another, change 519 to the
# display's logical width less 1188. Each rule applies only as a window
# opens, so either can be moved after.
#
# Where the two overlap, as on a narrower screen, tcs-sim's window is the
# one on top: the MOC's opens with "Keep below other windows" set, which
# its window menu turns off.
#
# The first rule places tcs-sim's window wherever it opens, with or without
# a lander; leave it out where tcs-sim runs beside tcs-moc and the two are
# to be placed some other way.

[TCS Payload Simulator]
Description=TCS Payload Simulator at the top right
position=519,0
positionrule=3
title=TCS Payload Simulator
titlematch=1
types=1
wmclassmatch=0

[TCS Lander MOC]
Description=TCS Lander MOC at the top left, below the TCS Payload Simulator
position=0,0
positionrule=3
below=true
belowrule=3
title=TCS Lander MOC
titlematch=1
types=1
wmclassmatch=0
